==Trivia==
*Enma is the Japanese name of [[wikipedia:Yama (Buddhism)|Yama]], a deity in East Asian and Buddhist mythology.
**Lord Enma is the elephant, not the [[Doge]]. The beard, eyebrows and headwear are common traits in depictions of Enma.
**This isn't the only time Enma has appeared as an enemy in a [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]] tower defense game: In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou]], the final boss of [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Jigoku|Jigoku]] Chapter 1 is [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Enma-Daiō|Enma-Daiō]].
*The kanji on Lord Enma's headwear is 王, meaning king/emperor.
**This detail is shared with [[Hell Warden Emma (Uber Rare Cat)|Hell Warden Emma]], a character that also references the god Yama.
*Lord Enma may have been inspired by the [https://youtu.be/xRwIykRc5Dw red elephants] of [[wikipedia:Tsavo|Tsavo]], Kenya, whose skin gains a red hue from the iron oxide-rich soil that accumulates on them. These distinctive elephants are one of the most iconic features of [https://www.britannica.com/place/Tsavo-National-Park Tsavo National Park].

